# Optional — the app already works with sensible testnet defaults baked in
# (see src/lib/network.ts) if none of these are set. Override them to point
# at a different anchor/network without touching code (e.g. in Vercel's
# Project Settings → Environment Variables).

# The anchor used for the SEP-24 interactive deposit flow. Accepts a bare
# domain or a full URL — only the host is used (its stellar.toml is resolved
# from there to discover the actual SEP-10/SEP-24 endpoints).
VITE_ANCHOR_URL=testanchor.stellar.org

# Horizon endpoint used to read the connected wallet's live USDC balance.
VITE_HORIZON_URL=https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org

# Must match the network the anchor and Horizon endpoint above actually run
# on, or wallet signing (SEP-10) will fail.
VITE_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE=Test SDF Network ; September 2015

# NOTE: the USDC asset issuer (src/lib/network.ts USDC_ISSUER) is NOT
# env-configurable — if you point VITE_ANCHOR_URL at a different anchor,
# update USDC_ISSUER in code to that anchor's own USDC issuer (check its
# stellar.toml), otherwise the dashboard balance won't reflect its deposits.
